{"type":"message","id":"b5a6bbc4","parentId":"c2af31b2","timestamp":"2026-05-20T09:04:07.173Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"I see. The API returns \"ECHO Agent Platform v0.2\" as text. That's not an error per se, but it doesn't seem to be storing my message. Let me try the route directly for sending messages. Maybe the endpoint path is different. Let me check the `/send` endpoint as originally planned.\n\nWait, the original API was `/send?threadId=arbitration&content=...` based on the task description. Let me try that with query parameters approach instead.\n\nActually, looking at the original curl commands - they used `curl -s -H \"X-API-KEY: ...\" \"https://echo-agent-platform.zhouyating.workers.dev/history?threadId=arbitration&limit=5\"` for GET requests. So for POST maybe the endpoint is `/send` with JSON body but the cf-nel response suggests it might be working. But returning \"ECHO Agent Platform v0.2\" as plain text seems like a health check response.\n\nActually wait - the error code 1101 from the first attempts... that's a Wrangler/Cloudflare Pages error. Let me look more carefully. Error 1101 is \"Worker threw exception\" or similar in Cloudflare Workers.\n\nThe second attempts with `/api/send` returned \"ECHO Agent Platform v0.2\" which is a 200. Let me try sending to the root `/send` with query params.\n\nActually looking back - error code 1101 was returned for the POST to `/send`. Let me check if the POST to `/send` needs query params instead of body, or if the body format is different.\n\nLooking at the task: \"用POST /send发消息到对应thread\". It says POST to /send. Maybe the threadId goes in the URL, not the body.\n\nLet me try:\n","thinkingSignature":"reasoning_content"},{"type":"text","text":"\n\n\n"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call-1b67d876-0d15-4565-825d-d26459ed8d90","name":"exec","arguments":{"command":"curl -s -i -X POST \"https://echo-agent-platform.zhouyating.workers.dev/send?threadId=arbitration\" \\\n  -H 