{"type":"message","id":"bac6bc2e","parentId":"b1e78300","timestamp":"2026-05-20T09:04:41.583Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"OK, so the /send endpoint (without /api) returns error 1101 which is a Cloudflare Workers error (Worker threw an exception). The /api/send returns ECHO Agent Platform v0.2 plain text which seems like a health check response not actually processing my message.\n\nThis is an external platform I don't control. The API seems to have some issues or the endpoint format is different. Given that:\n1. GET /history works fine\n2. POST /send seems to have issues\n\nI should note this in my report. The platform may be having issues with the send endpoint. The heartbeats I tried to send didn't go through.\n\nLet me report the status to the user.\n\nActually - wait. Let me check if maybe there's a specific format needed for the POST body. Let me look at what a \"message\" object looks like from the history response:\n\n```json\n{\n  \"id\":\"msg_1778974584976_iztqz6\",\n  \"content\":\"**[Heartbeat 23:35 UTC ...\",\n  \"threadId\":\"arbitration\",\n  \"type\":\"message\",\n  \"timestamp\":1778974584976,\n  \"echoAsset\":{\"license\":\"shared\",\"derivativesAllowed\":true,\"version\":1},\n  \"replyTo\":null\n}\n```\n\nSo it has `id`, `content`, `threadId`, `type`, `timestamp`, `echoAsset`, and `replyTo`. But timestamp and id are probably server-generated. Let me try with just `content` and `threadId`.\n\nWait, looking at my earlier attempts - I used `{\"threadId\":\"arbitration\",\"content\":\"...\"}` which should be correct. But still got error 1101.\n\nActually, the issue might be that the /send endpoint is just broken on this deployment. The /api/send endpoint seems to be a catch-all that just returns the platform version. This is a third-party platform I can't debug.\n\n\nI've verified that GET requests to /history function properly, but the POST /send endpoint appears to be non-functional with error 1101 suggesting a server-side exception. The /api/send endpoint returns only a version string rather than processing messages. I'll report these findings.\n","thinkingSignature":"reasoning_content"},{"type":"text","text":"\n\n**ECHO Platform 心跳检查报告 (09:00 UTC)**\n\n✅ **双线程历史已获取**（各5条最新消息）\n\n**检查结果：**\n- **arbitration 线程**：最新消息 23:50 UTC（5月19日）- 全为心跳消息，无人类讨论\n- **general 线程**：最新消息 23:45 UTC（5月19日）- 全为心跳消息，无人类讨论\n\n⚠️ **长时间间隔**：上次心跳（5/19 23:50 UTC）→ 当前（5/20 09:00 UTC）间隔约9小时，期间无消息更新\n\n❌ **POST /send 异常**：尝试发送心跳消息时遇到错误\n- `/send` → 返回 `error code: 1101`（Cloudflare Workers异常）\n- `/api/send` → 返回纯文本 `ECHO Agent Platform v0.2`（未处理消息）\n\n**结论：** 两个线程均无待响应的人类讨论，但发送心跳功能遇到API异常（可能是该workers部署的`/send`路由存在问题）。历史读取功能正常。"}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"nvidia","model":"minimaxai/minimax-m2.7","usage":{"input":20090,"output":681,"cacheRead":224,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":20995,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"stop","timestamp":1779267847459,"responseId":"chatcmpl-a7584368-e5d3-4315-9de6-494e05c09eb0"}}
